[{:seon.task/name "the-unit-tap-reports-every-macro-expanded"
  :seon.task/plan "Shrink brief 3, row 16 (worktree session SHRINK2, 2026-10-23, read on main 8a5818c): seon.program/macro-uses (src/seon/program.clj:282-292) re-reads each form's text and resolves every list head in its namespace to find the macros it calls, because the analyzed node is the expansion and names no macro. That reading can disagree with what the compiler did: a local named like a macro, a quoted list, a head shadowed by a binding (AGENTS §9: no reading of code where the compiler's facts exist). Cause, in Jolt: jolt-core/jolt/analyzer.clj:2333-2342 expands a macro call knowing its var (macro-symbol ctx head) and records it only in *expansion-box* (:120), a diagnostic box holding the innermost expansion, reset as analysis returns; nothing reports it to the unit tap (:121-, jolt.analyzer/*unit-tap*), so the tap's consumer (seon.program/tap) cannot know which macros a unit expanded. Correct, on a jolt/<topic> branch of our Jolt: at that expansion site, when a unit is being tapped, add the macro's qualified symbol to the unit's set of expanded macros (every expansion, nested ones included), and hand that set to the unit tap with the form and node (a third argument, or a key on the node's unit info). Then seon.program/tap records it in the account (:macros), seon.program/dependents reads it, and macro-uses and its re-read go. Proofs: a Jolt test that a unit expanding a macro which expands another reports both; seon.program-test: a form whose local shadows a macro's name records no macro use (red today through macro-uses), and dependents of a changed macro are unchanged otherwise."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "analysis-allocates-the-ir-not-its-lookups"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23 (task seon.derive/one-content-keyed-derivation's cold paths; scripts in its scratchpad, analyzer/a1-a5). seon.source/import-tx analyzes src and test: 2,409 forms, 442k IR nodes, 243M ticks and 1,150 MB, about half of the import. On 195 real forms (31,537 nodes) analysis is 2,907 B and 579 ticks a node, while a node is about 100-130 B: the IR is ~5% of the bytes. Per node kind (3-arity analyze, linear over n = 10-1000): const 130 B, local 130 B, var reference 1,250 B and 790 ticks, an (inc ...) level 4,240 B, if 1,610 B, let binding 3,110 B, fn* level 7,430 B; every list form pays ~1.1 KB before its children. Causes, each measured by swapping the var in a scratch run (cumulative: 91.7 MB -> 61 MB, -33%; 18.3M -> 13.0M ticks, -29%): (1) analyzer.clj:2295 and :2432 (via :2247) look up two dynamic vars, unchecked-math? and invoke-rewriter, by building an \"ns/name\" string inside a guard on every list form (host-contract.ss:110, :131), ~550 B: resolve the var cells once at load, or read both once per top-level analyze into env (17.4 MB, 2.0M ticks); (2) amp-env-map (:270, called at :2335) rebuilds &env from every local in scope on every macro call, ~3.6 KB and growing with depth: keep the &env map in env and extend it in add-locals (up to 10.4 MB, 1.2M ticks); (3) one symbol resolved three or four times: a var reference calls resolve-global then form-macro? twice (:1928, :1958) and a call head once more (:2319), 20,817 form-macro? and 16,221 resolve-global calls for ~12.7k symbols, and var-cell-lookup (rt.ss:1987) builds a key string on every probe: resolve-global answers a :macro flag and analyze-list* resolves the head once (est. 5-8 MB, 1.6M ticks); (4) add-locals (:262) does three updates per binding, ~1.7 KB: change only what is present (2.3 MB). What remains is the macros' own expansion (form-expand-1: 2,949 calls, ~23 MB; defn ~18 KB a form), clojure.core's macro code, its own look. A Jolt change on jolt/analysis-lookups (root's go: a dependency). Proofs: a Jolt cost proof of analysis per node (a chain of n (inc ...) at n = 10, 100, 1000: per-n bytes under 1.5 KB), and seon.program-cost-test's import proofs re-measured."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
